WEBVTT

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:21.730
Considering their gear,
they're part of some team.

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:24.191
It's the Special Forces' Black Rabbit.

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:27.361
<i>Those are the guys</i>
<i>that captured Tachibana.</i>

00:00:32.908 --> 00:00:36.578
<i>I never thought</i>
<i>they would chase us this far.</i>

00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:38.622
<i>Yuya Kanzaki!</i>

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:44.044
<i>This is the Ozanami Squad of the CAAC</i>
<i>Malignant Area Security Forces.</i>

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:47.673
<i>Release Aiko Tachibana</i>
<i>and surrender immediately.</i>

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:51.134
<i>If you do not obey,</i>
<i>we're prepared to use force.</i>

00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:52.594
<i>I repeat,</i>

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:57.182
<i>release Aiko Tachibana</i>
<i>and surrender immediately.</i>

00:00:58.141 --> 00:00:59.059
Kanzaki!

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.980
There's no response.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:10.779
Fire.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:13.073
What the hell?

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:17.119
-They fired!
-Into the Matter!

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:19.997
Are you kidding me?

00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:55.967
They've activated the Matter!

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.016
It worked!

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.228
No, it didn't.

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:09.773
-The Matter!
-Damn!

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.275
-Minase! Cover that flank!
-Yes, sir!

00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:13.860
I'm going to help.

00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:15.654
Shiraishi,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.865
I'll tell them that I've come willingly.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.952
It's pointless.
They're here to take you back.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.413
They don't care
if you came willingly or not.

00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:25.539
Really?

00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:27.791
Prepare to fire.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:31.378
We'll get the Type 36 to retreat
to the bridge entrance.

00:03:34.381 --> 00:03:36.758
One bipod has separated from the Beetle.

00:03:39.344 --> 00:03:40.303
Yuya Kanzaki!

00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:43.974
What's happening back there?

00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:47.728
Kanzaki...

00:03:55.444 --> 00:03:57.237
Why are you interfering?

00:03:57.821 --> 00:03:59.030
I told you before.

00:03:59.156 --> 00:04:02.784
We're on orders
to bring back Aiko Tachibana.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.162
We'll ask the questions here.

00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:08.039
What do you think you're doing?

00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:11.460
I'm here to end it all.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:14.087
There's something I have to do.

00:04:14.463 --> 00:04:16.965
Nothing's going to stop me.

00:04:17.048 --> 00:04:19.926
What do you mean by "all"?
State your purpose.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.053
There's no need.

00:04:22.345 --> 00:04:26.308
Even if I told you,
you people would never understand.

00:04:28.685 --> 00:04:29.686
Is that so?

00:04:30.771 --> 00:04:33.523
I know you can hear me, Aiko Tachibana.

00:04:36.693 --> 00:04:39.738
Why are you following this man?

00:04:40.238 --> 00:04:42.365
What do you know about Yuya Kanzaki?

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:44.910
I...

00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:49.790
His objective is unclear.
He'll only put you in terrible danger.

00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:52.793
Lives could be lost as well.

00:04:54.211 --> 00:04:56.797
<i>Let me ask you this, Aiko Tachibana.</i>

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:01.134
Why do you trust this man?

00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:14.564
It's the human form...

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:17.818
Ozanami...

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:21.154
Captain!

00:05:27.619 --> 00:05:29.204
Retreat!

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.545
It's going after the light.

00:05:36.962 --> 00:05:38.755
Turn off all your lights!

00:05:39.047 --> 00:05:40.674
What about our comms?

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:43.176
The fog is thin. Switch to radio!

00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:45.470
Cease fire!

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.475
The Matter is sensitive to light.

00:05:50.559 --> 00:05:51.685
Because it's night?

00:05:53.311 --> 00:05:54.813
<i>We can escape now!</i>

00:05:54.896 --> 00:05:57.732
But the tunnel is plugged with Matter!

00:05:57.899 --> 00:05:59.401
-Leave that to me!
-What?

00:05:59.985 --> 00:06:01.403
We'll use tracer bullets

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:03.488
to attract the Matter in the area,

00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:08.660
then the Beetle's grenade launcher

00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:12.247
to hit the exit at the far side
of the tunnel with a flare!

00:06:14.624 --> 00:06:18.420
The Matter inside the tunnel
will pull out upstream.

00:06:22.424 --> 00:06:25.176
Then, while it's chasing the light...

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.887
We'll chase it!

00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:33.894
We'll run for it once we're through!

00:06:34.686 --> 00:06:36.813
There's Matter here!

00:06:37.522 --> 00:06:39.816
There's some large Matter up ahead.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:47.073
No way!

00:06:54.497 --> 00:06:56.333
<i>We can't attack if it's on the gate.</i>

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:59.419
Spread out
and draw it away from the Beetle!

00:06:59.836 --> 00:07:02.547
I'll send out two automated
bipods as decoys.

00:07:03.214 --> 00:07:04.341
Deploy!

00:07:46.841 --> 00:07:48.468
It's all right, Tachibana.

00:07:49.219 --> 00:07:50.178
This way!

00:07:54.391 --> 00:07:55.684
Let's do this!

00:07:59.562 --> 00:08:01.648
<i>The upstream side is also active!</i>

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:23.545
I knew it wouldn't work.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:31.553
-Now!
-Now!

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:46.901
<i>Kanzaki, are you okay?</i>

00:08:46.985 --> 00:08:50.030
We're okay. It stopped moving.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.784
Carbon hardening? Why?

00:08:55.285 --> 00:08:57.495
Tachibana! Are you okay?

00:08:57.704 --> 00:08:59.706
Yes.

00:09:11.676 --> 00:09:12.552
Tachibana!

00:09:15.805 --> 00:09:16.931
It's over.

00:09:20.351 --> 00:09:21.811
<i>The Ozanami Squad?</i>

00:09:21.936 --> 00:09:22.812
<i>Yes.</i>

00:09:22.896 --> 00:09:27.817
<i>Final communication with them</i>
<i>was at 3:27 a.m. from Moriishi Point.</i>

00:09:29.694 --> 00:09:31.571
<i>If their operations hit a wall,</i>

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:34.741
<i>Nanbara's sure to try</i>
<i>something else soon.</i>

00:09:35.283 --> 00:09:38.078
<i>She doesn't want to lose Aiko Tachibana.</i>

00:09:39.621 --> 00:09:40.830
<i>I'll handle things here.</i>

00:09:41.414 --> 00:09:42.540
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:09:44.292 --> 00:09:48.338
<i>We also ran into human form Matter</i>
<i>at the Atobiki Bridge.</i>

00:09:48.963 --> 00:09:51.800
<i>Is it the same type</i>
<i>that you faced in Unazuki?</i>

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:52.884
<i>And Evidence?</i>

00:09:53.468 --> 00:09:54.969
<i>It's not in there yet.</i>

00:09:55.929 --> 00:09:58.473
<i>It could be derived from normal Matter.</i>

00:09:59.182 --> 00:10:02.435
<i>But I can't understand</i>
<i>why it would take that shape.</i>

00:10:03.061 --> 00:10:06.022
What? Both teams passed the competition?

00:10:06.106 --> 00:10:07.273
Come on, Shino!

00:10:07.357 --> 00:10:10.026
What was the point
in having the competition?

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.613
Does it matter? We passed.

00:10:13.696 --> 00:10:16.908
Anyway, looking forward
to having you around, Aiko.

00:10:17.242 --> 00:10:18.118
What?

00:10:20.328 --> 00:10:21.496
Yes.

00:10:22.831 --> 00:10:24.999
Let me revise what I said before.

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:28.878
I need all of you for this mission.

00:10:30.004 --> 00:10:31.381
Will you accept it?

00:10:36.261 --> 00:10:37.971
Yes, of course.

00:10:38.096 --> 00:10:39.264
We'll accept it.

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:42.809
Jeez! These guys are coming, too?

00:10:42.892 --> 00:10:46.020
Stop complaining.
You know you're happy about it.

00:10:46.104 --> 00:10:48.231
Hey! I am not!

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:50.525
Wow! You're unusually honest.

00:10:53.194 --> 00:10:54.988
<i>-Thanks.</i>
<i>-For what?</i>

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.740
<i>If I hadn't gotten this mission,</i>

00:10:57.824 --> 00:11:00.785
I never could have imagined
going this deep

00:11:00.869 --> 00:11:02.495
into the Area again.

00:11:02.871 --> 00:11:04.330
That's how I feel.

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:07.041
We finally made it back here

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:11.087
for the first time
since we quit Special Forces.

00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:12.964
That's right.

00:11:13.464 --> 00:11:16.551
And the real fight is still to come.

00:11:16.634 --> 00:11:18.261
You're right.

00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:26.728
Stop! Cease fire!

00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:38.781
We'll leave as soon as
the vehicles are charged,

00:11:38.948 --> 00:11:40.283
Try to get some sleep.

00:11:42.368 --> 00:11:43.661
Is something wrong?

00:11:44.245 --> 00:11:48.207
Can we reconsider our future plans?

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.418
What do you mean?

00:11:51.628 --> 00:11:55.131
We can't take everyone
any farther than this.

00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:58.051
We must not!

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:03.556
I wonder what the hell the objective is.

00:12:03.932 --> 00:12:06.017
It has nothing to do with us.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:07.477
Yes, it does!

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.063
I mean, Aiko seemed...

00:12:10.688 --> 00:12:12.482
pretty depressed.

00:12:13.775 --> 00:12:15.944
She saw people die.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.946
That's a shocking thing to see.

00:12:20.073 --> 00:12:22.992
All the reason more to protect her.

00:12:24.827 --> 00:12:25.703
Roger, that.

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:27.622
<i>They can't go.</i>

00:12:28.498 --> 00:12:31.626
Kazuki, Kaede, and the others.

00:12:32.085 --> 00:12:35.797
I can't put them in danger for our sake.

00:12:36.089 --> 00:12:38.466
They knew the danger coming into this.

00:12:38.716 --> 00:12:41.803
But, after what happened on the bridge...

00:12:42.011 --> 00:12:44.389
If you get to Primary Point,

00:12:44.555 --> 00:12:46.265
the Burst can be stopped.

00:12:46.891 --> 00:12:50.812
We'll return your duplicate body
and rescue your family.

00:12:51.187 --> 00:12:53.189
We'll solve everything.

00:12:53.898 --> 00:12:57.652
Is it really all right
to put everyone in danger for that?

00:12:58.111 --> 00:12:59.278
I don't think so.

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:02.657
That would never make Mom or Ryota happy.

00:13:08.037 --> 00:13:11.416
I can't get everyone involved.
I can't take them farther!

00:13:11.874 --> 00:13:13.501
Those other people don't matter!

00:13:15.503 --> 00:13:18.464
I want to save Aiko Tachibana.

00:13:20.425 --> 00:13:22.844
But why?

00:13:26.347 --> 00:13:28.975
I can't understand this, Kanzaki.

00:13:33.521 --> 00:13:35.898
<i>We're all headed for the same place.</i>

00:13:35.982 --> 00:13:39.027
<i>Do we have to keep it</i>
<i>a secret from everyone?</i>

00:13:41.612 --> 00:13:43.781
I want to tell everyone the reason

00:13:44.574 --> 00:13:46.034
we're going to Ground Zero,

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.996
and that my body, except for my brain,

00:13:50.621 --> 00:13:52.957
is made entirely of artificial organisms.

00:13:54.375 --> 00:13:55.960
<i>I want them to know everything.</i>

00:14:00.506 --> 00:14:05.303
I deleted the data you told me to
from the Kiryu Hospital server.

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:06.763
Thanks for that.

00:14:07.138 --> 00:14:10.141
I found something interesting
while I was in there.

00:14:10.433 --> 00:14:11.476
You did?

00:14:12.268 --> 00:14:14.103
These are a patient's vitals.

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:18.649
Zero consciousness level?
What's wrong with this patient?

00:14:18.733 --> 00:14:22.403
It's not my field, so I can't really tell,

00:14:22.653 --> 00:14:26.783
but when you trace her brainwaves,
they match up with certain events.

00:14:27.158 --> 00:14:30.161
For example, July 23.

00:14:30.661 --> 00:14:32.663
The day the Matter became active.

00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:34.165
And...

00:14:34.248 --> 00:14:35.917
here's the patient.

00:14:37.168 --> 00:14:38.252
Yuzuha!

00:14:38.336 --> 00:14:39.545
You know her?

00:14:40.129 --> 00:14:44.550
She's the only daughter of Kyosuke Isazu,
an artificial organism developer.

00:14:45.468 --> 00:14:47.303
What the hell is going on here?

00:14:48.221 --> 00:14:52.433
Are Yuzuha's brain activity
and the Matter's activity linked?

00:14:53.142 --> 00:14:54.352
This is bad.

00:14:54.519 --> 00:14:57.855
This is something
that Yuya never imagined!

00:14:59.732 --> 00:15:01.025
Dr. Kiryu,

00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:03.945
the Cell Assembler that you developed,

00:15:04.821 --> 00:15:08.324
and the further development by Yura
of Cell Assembler Two,

00:15:08.408 --> 00:15:13.079
have been on ice for a long time.
I'm starting research on them again.

00:15:14.038 --> 00:15:15.581
I see.

00:15:16.207 --> 00:15:18.918
It's the future of humanity.

00:15:19.502 --> 00:15:23.423
We need it to deal with the Burst,
and to make progress.

00:15:24.882 --> 00:15:27.093
Leave it to me.

00:15:29.762 --> 00:15:31.806
Even without Yura...

00:15:31.889 --> 00:15:34.350
and without the Yura Notes...

00:15:35.059 --> 00:15:37.311
I swear that I will save you.

00:15:39.647 --> 00:15:42.692
I know you can hear me, Yuzuha.

00:15:43.901 --> 00:15:45.194
<i>Dad!</i>

00:15:48.322 --> 00:15:50.074
Dad!

00:15:50.867 --> 00:15:52.326
Headed home from school?

00:15:52.535 --> 00:15:53.494
Yes.

00:15:54.829 --> 00:15:55.746
Dr. Yura!

00:15:56.789 --> 00:15:58.082
Yuzuha.

00:15:58.291 --> 00:16:01.210
Do you remember your promise for today?

00:16:01.669 --> 00:16:03.921
What was it?

00:16:04.213 --> 00:16:08.342
You said you'd listen to me
play the violin!

00:16:08.593 --> 00:16:10.636
Oh, that's right.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:13.473
I practiced really hard, you know.

00:16:20.855 --> 00:16:22.648
Dr. Yura?

00:16:22.732 --> 00:16:25.526
Go ahead. Let me hear it.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.570
What? Here?

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:57.141
The area for the rest of this mission,
from K2 until Primary Point,

00:16:57.391 --> 00:17:03.314
hasn't been visited since the CAAC
Special Forces pulled out.

00:17:03.898 --> 00:17:05.274
Stay on your guard!

00:17:07.026 --> 00:17:10.530
<i>I can see the Number Two</i>
<i>Power Plant at the relay point.</i>

00:17:11.948 --> 00:17:13.950
There's activity on the rail line!

00:17:14.033 --> 00:17:16.118
The railway ahead is blocked!

00:17:16.244 --> 00:17:17.161
Evidence?

00:17:17.245 --> 00:17:19.455
No previous contact. It's a new type!

00:17:19.956 --> 00:17:22.083
Have you found out anything?

00:17:22.166 --> 00:17:25.086
No. As we get closer to Primary Point,

00:17:25.545 --> 00:17:27.880
the contact field produced by the Matter

00:17:27.964 --> 00:17:29.799
is getting stronger.

00:17:30.091 --> 00:17:32.260
It's hard to even get a signal now.

00:17:32.843 --> 00:17:36.514
I wonder if her consciousness level there
is decreasing even more.

00:17:36.597 --> 00:17:40.768
We have to reach her
before it completely disappears.

00:17:40.851 --> 00:17:43.145
And then there's her reaction.

00:17:47.817 --> 00:17:50.653
We may have less time than I thought.

00:17:51.279 --> 00:17:52.572
It's coming!

00:17:52.655 --> 00:17:53.823
What?

00:17:55.116 --> 00:17:56.158
What?

00:17:56.284 --> 00:17:59.036
<i>The railway's blocked!</i>
<i>Bringing in the Beetle!</i>

00:18:05.793 --> 00:18:07.670
The activity is too widespread!

00:18:08.045 --> 00:18:09.714
Pull back behind the Beetle!

00:18:10.256 --> 00:18:13.092
Cover us with the heavy laser
until we clear the way!

00:18:13.175 --> 00:18:14.051
Roger!

00:18:14.594 --> 00:18:16.178
I'll fire the laser.

00:18:16.554 --> 00:18:19.348
Kazuki, I made a ton
of Matter fragments!

00:18:19.432 --> 00:18:21.392
I found some crystallized Matter!

00:18:22.602 --> 00:18:23.477
Got it!

00:18:25.855 --> 00:18:27.023
Here it comes, Kanzaki!

00:18:27.106 --> 00:18:28.608
<i>I sent you the data!</i>

00:18:28.691 --> 00:18:30.651
Take over the laser, Shiraishi.

00:18:30.735 --> 00:18:31.569
Roger!

00:18:31.652 --> 00:18:32.987
It's coming again!

00:18:33.821 --> 00:18:34.697
Matter?

00:18:35.781 --> 00:18:36.782
It's under us?!

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.621
Aiko, are you okay?

00:18:41.746 --> 00:18:42.747
Yes.

00:18:49.587 --> 00:18:50.755
Aiko?

00:18:50.838 --> 00:18:51.839
What are you...

00:18:51.922 --> 00:18:53.215
I'll take the laser.

00:18:53.299 --> 00:18:54.216
Tachibana!

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:56.927
If we're doing this,
then I'm fighting, too!

00:18:57.553 --> 00:19:00.181
I don't want anyone to die!

00:19:11.901 --> 00:19:12.902
Aiko!

00:19:12.985 --> 00:19:14.028
Finished!

00:19:18.157 --> 00:19:19.617
<i>I sent the cartridges!</i>

00:19:20.868 --> 00:19:21.994
Here goes another!

00:19:25.289 --> 00:19:26.248
Again!

00:19:28.125 --> 00:19:29.794
-It's Matter!
-Kanzaki!

00:19:35.675 --> 00:19:37.009
Aiko, get down!

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.940
-Kanzaki!
-Tachibana!

00:20:29.478 --> 00:20:30.396
<i>What is this?</i>

00:20:39.947 --> 00:20:41.115
Gummi?

00:21:07.767 --> 00:21:08.851
Aiko!

00:21:09.977 --> 00:21:11.312
-Tachibana!
-Aiko!

00:21:11.937 --> 00:21:14.190
Kanzaki, I'll get her out with the Beetle!

00:21:14.273 --> 00:21:15.274
What happened?

00:21:15.399 --> 00:21:18.152
<i>Aiko is buried under crystallized Matter.</i>

00:21:18.235 --> 00:21:19.695
-What?
-What?

00:21:19.779 --> 00:21:22.865
-No way!
-I'll use the Beetle to get her out.

00:21:22.948 --> 00:21:27.620
<i>Everyone, your job is to tranquilize</i>
<i>the Matter with the synthesized chemicals!</i>

00:21:27.703 --> 00:21:29.246
This can't be happening!

00:21:31.457 --> 00:21:32.458
Tachibana!

00:21:33.834 --> 00:21:37.296
<i>Active Matter cleared.</i>
<i>Beetle's path secured.</i>

00:21:38.047 --> 00:21:38.881
Aiko!

00:21:38.964 --> 00:21:40.174
Is she all right?

00:21:40.257 --> 00:21:42.635
They're both outside without suits?

00:21:48.057 --> 00:21:52.061
Hey! What the hell is going on?

00:21:52.353 --> 00:21:55.064
Those are carbon nanostructures.

00:21:55.189 --> 00:21:58.651
But, I thought that only happened
to artificial organisms.

00:21:59.068 --> 00:22:00.736
I'll clean her in the bipod.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:04.865
Clean her? But she's not wearing a suit.

00:22:05.282 --> 00:22:06.325
It's all right.

00:22:07.076 --> 00:22:09.787
She's not a normal human.

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:10.746
-What?
-What?

00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:13.499
She's a composite.

00:22:14.124 --> 00:22:18.379
A composite of a real brain
and an artificial organism body.

00:22:19.964 --> 00:22:21.590
Aiko is a composite?

00:22:21.674 --> 00:22:23.384
Is that even possible?

00:22:27.096 --> 00:22:30.099
Hey, if that's true,
it means the whole time

00:22:30.474 --> 00:22:32.851
we've been in the Area,

00:22:32.977 --> 00:22:35.813
we've been dragging Matter bait with us.

00:24:09.865 --> 00:24:11.951
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
